## Final Verdict: Which Clarity Should You Buy?

**Buyer 1 — Online buyer, no photo access:** Buy VS1 minimum, no exceptions. The clarity works in all lighting conditions without verification. At 1ct natural, [E-VS1 at $2,464](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/28919719?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) is the benchmark. At 2ct natural, [F-VS1 at $21,213](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/27103709?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) is the floor. Do not compromise to save money you will regret when the stone arrives.

**Buyer 2 — Budget-conscious with photo access:** VS2 is conditionally available if you receive and review high-resolution overhead photos before buying. Look for inclusions away from the table center. If the retailer cannot provide photos, move to VS1 and do not look back. The [E-VS2 1.01ct at $2,743](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/28958820?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) can work — but only after photo review confirms safe inclusion position.

**Buyer 3 — Lab-grown buyer:** There is almost no budget case for going below VS1 in lab asscher. The [1.52ct D-IF at $2,795](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/27991043?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) gives you flawless clarity in a 1.5ct stone for near 1ct natural price. At 2ct lab, [D-FL at $5,510](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/29446220?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) is not meaningfully more than VS1 options. Buy high clarity in lab — the price penalty is minimal and the step facets will reward it every time you look at the stone.

**Buyer 4 — Large stone at 3ct+:** At 3ct+, VS1 is not enough. Move to VVS2 as your floor for natural stones. The large step facets on a 3ct asscher amplify inclusions more dramatically than at 1–2ct. Natural [F-VVS2 3.26ct at $36,991](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/28507345?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) is the right natural entry at this size. Lab [D-IF 3ct at $8,849](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/26682894?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) gives maximum clarity for 24% of natural cost.

> **Farzana says:** The asscher cut is the most honest diamond shape you can buy. That's what makes it beautiful. And it's exactly what makes clarity so important. You cannot hide behind the sparkle here. The mirrored corridors show you everything — the architecture, the depth, the precision of the cut. And every inclusion you accept. Buy VS1 in asscher and you'll never second-guess the stone. Buy SI1 and you'll see it every time the light hits right.

---

## Expert Summary

Asscher cut diamond clarity is not negotiable the way it is in brilliant cuts. The step-cut facets that create the hall-of-mirrors effect also eliminate the optical cover that hides inclusions in round, oval, and cushion diamonds. Every flaw in an asscher sits inside a clean mirror — visible, positioned, and potentially multiplied by the Mirror Multiplication Effect.

The practical rules are simple. VS1 is the starting grade for confident asscher buyers. VS2 is available only with individual stone photo review.

SI1 is almost never eye-clean in asscher and should be avoided without expert verification and video. At 2ct and above, VS1 becomes the hard floor — the Clarity Floor Rule moves the minimum grade up as the stone size increases because larger step facets expose inclusions more dramatically.

For natural GIA buyers, the most efficient clarity entries are [E-VS1 at $2,464](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/28919719?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) at 1ct and [F-VS1 at $21,213](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/27103709?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) at 2ct. For lab buyers, the [1.52ct D-IF at $2,795](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/27991043?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) represents the strongest clarity value in the category — flawless clarity in a 1.5ct stone for near the price of a 1ct natural VS1.

The step-cut format rewards buyers who invest in clarity. The hall-of-mirrors effect, the clean geometric depth, the long light corridors — all of these become more beautiful, not less, when the stone is free of visible inclusions.

For the full picture of what makes an asscher perform optically, see the [ideal proportions guide](/asscher-cut-diamond-ideal-proportions). For setting recommendations that complement high-clarity step cuts, see the [engagement ring guide](/asscher-cut-diamond-engagement-rings).

